Running miniAMR...
** Error ** Unknown input parameter --log
(Optional) command line input is of the form: 

--nx - block size x (even && > 0)
--ny - block size y (even && > 0)
--nz - block size z (even && > 0)
--init_x - initial blocks in x (> 0)
--init_y - initial blocks in y (> 0)
--init_z - initial blocks in z (> 0)
--reorder - ordering of blocks if initial number > 1
--npx - (0 < npx <= num_pes)
--npy - (0 < npy <= num_pes)
--npz - (0 < npz <= num_pes)
--max_blocks - maximun number of blocks per core
--num_refine - (>= 0) number of levels of refinement
--block_change - (>= 0) number of levels a block can change in a timestep
--uniform_refine - if 1, then grid is uniformly refined
--refine_freq - frequency (in timesteps) of checking for refinement
--target_active - (>= 0) target number of blocks per core, none if 0
--target_max - (>= 0) max number of blocks per core, none if 0
--target_min - (>= 0) min number of blocks per core, none if 0
--inbalance - percentage inbalance to trigger inbalance
--lb_opt - load balancing - 0 = none, 1 = each refine, 2 = each refine phase
--num_vars - number of variables (> 0)
--comm_vars - number of vars to communicate together
--num_tsteps - number of timesteps (> 0)
--time - time to run problem with delta by object speed (> 0.0)
--stages_per_ts - number of comm/calc stages per timestep
--checksum_freq - number of stages between checksums
--stencil - 0 (variable work) or 7 or 27 point (27 will not work with refinement (except uniform))
--error_tol - (e^{-error_tol} ; >= 0) 
--report_diffusion - report check sums for each variable
--report_perf - 0, 1, 2
--plot_freq - frequency (timesteps) of plotting (0 for none)
--code - closely minic communication of different codes
         0 minimal sends, 1 send ghosts, 2 send ghosts and process on send
--permute - altenates directions in communication
--blocking_send - use blocking sends instead of nonblocking
--refine_ghost - use full extent of block (including ghosts) to determine if block is refined
--num_objects - (>= 0) number of objects to cause refinement
--object - type, position, movement, size, size rate of change
All associated settings are integers except for objects
